Looking at the crash in more detail, I inspected the contents of `PhpParser\Node\Stmt\Do_` in https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/blob/38c452ae584467e939d55377aaf83b5a26f19dd1/src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/StatementsAnalyzer.php#L497-L499 by adding a try-catch:

```php
        } elseif ($stmt instanceof PhpParser\Node\Stmt\Do_) {
            try {
                DoAnalyzer::analyze($statements_analyzer, [$stmt], $context);
            } catch (\Throwable $e) {
                \error_log((new PhpParser\PrettyPrinter\Standard())->prettyPrint($stmt));
                throw $e;
            }
```

The actual code in `$stmt` there is:

```php
do {
    $response = $this->client->get($this->endpoint, $batchCriteria->toArray());
    $this->requestedCriteria->limit = $this->requestedCriteria->limit ?? 0;
    /** @psalm-var list<array> $items */
    $items = ($this->collectionParser)($response);
    if ([] === $items) {
        break;
    }
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        if ($this->requestedCriteria->limit <= $fetchedItems) {
            break;
        }
        (yield $itemParser($item));
        ++$fetchedItems;
    }
    $batchCriteria->page = ++$currentPage;
} while ($this->requestedCriteria->limit > $fetchedItems);
```

The problem seems to occur because `$this->requestedCriteria` is modified within the loop, when a `break;` occurs, but I'm unsure how to reproduce the issue in isolation :thinking:

I need an implementation like this. (I have to because of third party libraries). The getInstance function promises that it will return static(not self), that is child class, because Core is abstract (self is wrong). And in my opinion there is no logical error or ambiguity here that psalm showing the warnings MoreSpecificReturnType and LessSpecificReturnStatement 

```php
<?php

require_once('./vendor/autoload.php');

abstract class Core
{
    protected string $message;

    public function __construct()
    {
        $this->message = '"__construct"';
    }

    public static function getInstance(): static
    {
        /** @psalm-suppress UnsafeInstantiation */
        $self = new static();

        $self->message = $self->message . ' and "hi from Core"';

        return $self;
    }
}

class Child1 extends Core
{
    /** @psalm-suppress MoreSpecificReturnType */
    public static function getInstance(): static
    {
        $self = parent::getInstance();

        $self->message = $self->message . ' and "hi from Child"';

        /** @psalm-suppress LessSpecificReturnStatement */
        return $self;
    }
}

class Child2 extends Core
{
}

dump(new Child1());

dump((new Child1())->getInstance());

dump(new Child2());

dump((new Child2())->getInstance());

```

